From c73aa7b9f5e07b3b4bb34cbdfd947bd59c62840c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:10:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Bugfix: keep vertex labels of mesh files unchanged in
 `meshLoad()` [report PyScotch]

`meshLoad()` added the based number of the first vertex of each kind
(and the base adjustment) to every vertex label read from the file,
whereas `meshSave()` writes labels unchanged and edge ends as labels.
Loading and saving a labeled mesh therefore shifted all node labels by
`vnodbas` (and element labels when nodes come first), so that a mesh
file was not stable under `mcv`, labels in orderings and geometry
files no longer matched, and labeled files with a non-zero base could
not be loaded at all since their edge ends had to be labels plus the
base.

Store labels as read, as `graphLoad()` does, and treat edge ends of
labeled meshes as labels that `graphLoad2()` turns into vertex numbers.
Labels must then be unique across elements and nodes, which
`graphLoad2()` checks. Add a labeled mesh round trip to `check_prog_mcv`
and a labeled geometry file to `check_scotch_mesh_geom`.

Refs: PS2-G11-mesh-struct-io-5, SEP-16
